# Code owners for the vinuchain-lists repository.
#
# Lines below assign required reviewers to security-sensitive paths. GitHub
# requires the listed owners' approval before any PR touching these paths can be
# merged (once branch protection is configured to require code-owner review —
# see the repo settings; that is an org-admin action outside this file).
#
# The owner is the repository maintainer @ElemontCapital. To hand the gate to a
# team instead, create a GitHub team and replace @ElemontCapital below; a team
# distributes the review load and survives a single maintainer being away.

# Default owner for everything in the repo (data + code). Listing data paths
# (tokens/**, contracts/**, schemas/**) under an owner is what makes the
# "Manual Review — Maintainers verify legitimacy" promise enforceable against a
# malicious-but-checksummed entry substitution (AUD-01).
*                          @ElemontCapital

# CI workflow definitions — anything that runs with secrets attached.
.github/workflows/**       @ElemontCapital
.github/CODEOWNERS         @ElemontCapital
.github/dependabot.yml     @ElemontCapital

# Validator, on-chain checks, deployment, and oracle-update scripts. A malicious
# change here that slipped past review would run on the next scheduled VNS
# oracle update with the production private key in env, and validator changes
# silently weaken every other check.
scripts/**                 @ElemontCapital
schemas/**                 @ElemontCapital

# On-chain VNS contracts. Bytecode changes require a Solidity reviewer in
# addition to whoever ships the off-chain code.
contracts/vns/**           @ElemontCapital
